## 3. Control Loop Correctness — Full Trace

Tracing one complete loop iteration with realistic values:

```
Given: antenna at (23.810, 90.412), rover at (23.811, 90.413), heading = 45°

1. bearing = compute_bearing(23.810, 90.412, 23.811, 90.413)
   = atan2(sin(0.001°)×cos(23.811°), cos(23.810°)×sin(23.811°) - sin(23.810°)×cos(23.811°)×cos(0.001°))
   ≈ 41.8° (northeast)

2. distance = compute_distance(...) ≈ 148 meters

3. error = normalize(41.8 - 45.0) = -3.2°

4. deadband = compute_dynamic_deadband(148) = 148 × 0.01 = 1.48°
   apply_deadband(-3.2, 1.48) → fabs(-3.2) = 3.2 > 1.48 → returns -3.2 (full correction)

5. LPF: error = 0.2 × (-3.2) + 0.8 × prev_error
   If prev_error = 0: error = -0.64°

6. servo_angle = 90 + (-0.64) = 89.36°
   → clamp to [0, 180] → 89.36° ✅

7. set_servo_angle(89.36):
   → write_servo_raw(89.36)
     → us = 801 + (89.36/180) × 840 = 1218.1 µs
     → cur_servo_us = 1218 ← ISR protected ✅
     → write_servo_duty(pulse_to_duty(1218.1))
   → fabs(89.36 - 90.0) = 0.64 > 0.1 → pending=true, timer reset
   → cur_servo_angle = 89.36
   → pending=true but only 100ms elapsed → no NVS write yet ✅
```

**Result:** Servo rotates 0.64° counterclockwise. After multiple iterations, the LPF converges and the antenna tracks the rover. ✅

